  "result": "Here's a first draft (about 95 words). I haven't added it to `README.md` yet.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach shipping carrier is its own module in `shop/carriers/` (for example `acme.py` or `maple.py`). They're all registered in `REGISTRY` in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`, and you look one up by name with `shop.carriers.get(\"acme\")`.\n\nEach module sets a `BASE_RATE` (a flat fee in cents) plus a per-weight rate and a `ZONES` table of multipliers. `rate(weight, zone)` returns the quote in cents as an integer.\n\nMost carriers take the weight in **kilograms** (`PER_KG`, `MAX_KG`). The exception is **Maple** (`maple.py`), which takes it in **grams** (`PER_GRAMS`, `MAX_GRAMS`, up to 30000 g). Convert the weight before you ask Maple for a quote.\n```\n\nI checked the details against the code: there are 20 carriers, all define `BASE_RATE`, and `maple.py` is the only one that uses grams. Do you want me to add it to `README.md`?",
